[689.143466, "i", "cat > /workspace/tune3.py << 'EOF'\nimport torch\n\ntorch.manual_seed(0)\nM, N, K = 16384, 4096, 4096\nx32 = torch.rand(M, K, device=\"cuda\")\nw32 = (torch.rand(N, K, device=\"cuda\") * 2 - 1) / K ** 0.5 * 1.5\nb32 = torch.rand(N, device=\"cuda\") * 0.02\n\nwh = w32.half()\nwl = (w32 - wh.float()).half()\nwht = wh.t().contiguous()\nbh = b32.half()\nbl32 = b32 - bh.float()\n\ndef bench(f, iters=20):\n    for _ in range(5):\n        f()\n    torch.cuda.synchronize()\n    s = torch.cuda.Event(True); e = torch.cuda.Event(True)\n    dummy = torch.empty(32 * 1024 * 1024, dtype=torch.int64, device=\"cuda\")\n    times = []\n    for _ in range(iters):\n        dummy.fill_(42)\n        torch.cuda.synchronize()\n        s.record(); f(); e.record()\n        torch.cuda.synchronize()\n        times.append(s.elapsed_time(e))\n    times.sort()\n    return times[len(times)//2]\n\ndef compensated(x32):\n    xh = x32.half()\n    xl = (x32 - xh.float()).half()\n    m1 = torch.mm(xh, wht)                     # fp16 out, round err e1\n    e1 = m1.float() - torch.mm(xh.fl"]
[689.143529, "i", "oat(), wht.float())  # EXACT e1? too slow (fp32 mm)\n    return m1\n\n# exact e1 requires fp32 mm; instead compute e1 implicitly:\n# m2 = addmm(c, xl, wht) where c = bl32 - e1 must be known exactly. Not possible w/o fp32 mm.\n# Alternative: make ROUNDING exact by construction? No.\n# So: 3-GEMM compensated: m1 = mm(xh, wht); m2 = addmm(-(m1 - mmh?)...) not possible.\n# PRACTICAL: 3 GEMMs, m2 collects xl@wh + xh@wl - e1 where e1 = m1 - (m1 computed in fp32?) NO.\n# Simplest exact-residual trick: m2 = addmm(-m1.float()?? fp16 C...)\n# Test: m2 = torch.addmm(c16, xl, wht) with c16 = (-e1 + bl) fp16; e1 known only via fp32 mm -> dead end.\n# INSTEAD: 3rd GEMM captures xl@wh + xh@wl exactly in fp32 accum, and e1 is captured by\n# subtracting m1 in FP32: total = m1.float() + (m23.float() ... but m23 rounds too!\n# m23 = round16(xl@wh + xh@wl) has tiny magnitude (~1e-4 scale) so its rounding is ~6e-8. GOOD!\n# And e1 error from m1 remains ~ uniform [-0.0078, 0.0078]?? NO WAIT: final = m1 + m23 where\n# m1+m23 in fp32 is EXACT sum"]
[689.143545, "i", "; error = e1(round of m1) + e23(round of m23, ~1e-7).\n# e1 does NOT cancel. => This is same as hybrid 3mm which FAILED. Need e1 compensation:\n# m2 = addmm(C=-m1, ...) can't: C fp16 but m1 fp16 exact, -m1 exact in fp16! C=-m1 is exact!\n# m2 = round16(-m1 + xl@wh + xh@wl + bl)?? but then total = m1 + m2 = m1 + round(-m1 + small)\n# = m1 - m1 + small + e2 = small + e2. We LOSE the main term! Wrong algebra.\n# CORRECT compensation: m2 = round16( (xl@wh + xh@wl + bl32) - e1 ), e1 = m1 - exact(xh@wh+bh...)\n# exact xh@wh unavailable without fp32 mm. BUT: e1 = m1 - fp32(xh@wh); and fp32(xh@wh) = m1_exact.\n# Use mm with fp16 in fp32 out? torch.mm on fp16 gives fp16 out. BUT torch.matmul with\n# out_dtype? torch._scaled_mm? OR: run m1f = torch.mm(xh, wht) in fp16, and compute the SAME\n# product exactly via... xh, wh fp16 -> product EXACT in fp32 accumulate; if we could get fp32 out\n# we'd have exact m1 and e1 = m1 - m1exact. cuBLAS fp16 in fp32 out: torch.mm casts? Use\n# torch.matmul(xh, wht, out=fp32)? not allowed. BUT t"]
[689.14357, "i", "orch.addmm with beta=0 and fp32 out? dtype rules.\n# Solution: F.linear? No. USE torch._int_mm? No. cublasGemmEx via torch: mm with out dtype fp32:\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\nout32 = torch.empty(M, N, device='cuda', dtype=torch.float32)\ntry:\n    torch.mm(xh, wht, out=out32)\n    print('mm fp16->fp32 out: OK')\nexcept Exception as ex:\n    print('mm fp16->fp32 out FAIL:', ex)\nEOF\n"]
