[689.148764, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[689.148958, "o", "# INSTEAD: 3rd GEMM captures xl@wh + xh@wl exactly in fp32 accum, and e1 is captured by\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[689.149002, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[689.149177, "o", "# subtracting m1 in FP32: total = m1.float() + (m23.float() ... but m23 rounds too!\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[689.149215, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[689.14943, "o", "# m23 = round16(xl@wh + xh@wl) has tiny magnitude (~1e-4 scale) so its rounding is ~6e-8. GOOD!\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[689.149467, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[689.149678, "o", "# And e1 error from m1 remains ~ uniform [-0.0078, 0.0078]?? NO WAIT: final = m1 + m23 where\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[689.149716, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[689.149896, "o", "# m1+m23 in fp32 is EXACT sum; error = e1(round of m1) + e23(round of m23, ~1e-7).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[689.149935, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[689.150126, "o", "# e1 does NOT cancel. => This is same as hybrid 3mm which FAILED. Need e1 compensation:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[689.150157, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[689.150362, "o", "# m2 = addmm(C=-m1, ...) can't: C fp16 but m1 fp16 exact, -m1 exact in fp16! C=-m1 is exact!\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[689.150401, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[689.150611, "o", "# m2 = round16(-m1 + xl@wh + xh@wl + bl)?? but then total = m1 + m2 = m1 + round(-m1 + small)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[689.150649, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[689.150813, "o", "# = m1 - m1 + small + e2 = small + e2. We LOSE the main term! Wrong algebra.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[689.150853, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[689.151064, "o", "# CORRECT compensation: m2 = round16( (xl@wh + xh@wl + bl32) - e1 ), e1 = m1 - exact(xh@wh+bh...)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[689.151096, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[689.151314, "o", "# exact xh@wh unavailable without fp32 mm. BUT: e1 = m1 - fp32(xh@wh); and fp32(xh@wh) = m1_exact.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[689.151349, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[689.151542, "o", "# Use mm with fp16 in fp32 out? torch.mm on fp16 gives fp16 out. BUT torch.matmul with\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[689.151581, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[689.151777, "o", "# out_dtype? torch._scaled_mm? OR: run m1f = torch.mm(xh, wht) in fp16, and compute the SAME\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[689.151816, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[689.152041, "o", "# product exactly via... xh, wh fp16 -> product EXACT in fp32 accumulate; if we could get fp32 out\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[689.15208, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[689.152269, "o", "# we'd have exact m1 and e1 = m1 - m1exact. cuBLAS fp16 in fp32 out: torch.mm casts? Use\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[689.152308, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[689.152544, "o", "# torch.matmul(xh, wht, out=fp32)? not allowed. BUT torch.addmm with beta=0 and fp32 out? dtype rules.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[689.152582, "o", "> "]
[689.152789, "o", "# Solution: F.linear? No. USE torch._int_mm? No. cublasGemmEx via torch: mm with out dtype fp32:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[689.152829, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[689.15289, "o", "import torch.nn.functional as F\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[689.152928, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
